    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (80.64) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) headlining our offensive attack. **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against Taj Bradley; the combination of a favorable park, moderate SP skill, and elite sprint speed against a pitcher with a slow delivery provides maximum stolen base potential\u2014the primary currency of our strategy. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** is primed for a massive output facing Ure\u00f1a, where the park factor and dynamic platoon advantage push his efficiency well into elite territory. **Jose Caballero** (75.83) also presents an excellent value, as his strong platoon edge against Andrew Abbott and positive wind conditions make him an essential anchor in our middle infield.\n\nThe decision-making process required tough calls at the fringe, specifically regarding **Zach McKinstry**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 41.35. While **Zach McKinstry** offered a decent platoon edge against Sean Newcomb, his bottom-third batting order position and the high SP-xERA of Newcomb pushed his efficiency just below the threshold required to displace our current starters. We continue to monitor the status of **Mickey Moniak** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** on the IL, as their absence necessitates heavy reliance on depth pieces like **Max Muncy** (59.90), who remains a start based on the favorable park factors associated with the Ure\u00f1a matchup. \n\nRisk management remains a priority today, particularly regarding our left-handed bats. Both **Brice Turang** and **Josh Naylor** face significant headwinds due to elite SP-xERA matchups, resulting in suppressed scores of 45.62 and 47.12, respectively. While **Brice Turang** retains value through his top-of-the-order positioning, the matchup against Chris Sale demands we keep expectations tempered. We are keeping **Dalton Rushing** in the lineup despite a sub-50 score, banking on the wind-out conditions and his specific contact profile against the slow delivery of Triston Rogers to potentially overcome the order-slot disadvantage.",
